    {"problem": "The AC is 15 years old and the furnace isn't far behind", "solution": "When both units are near the end, replacing them together costs less than two separate jobs. A ducted cold-climate heat pump can take the place of the air conditioner and do most of the heating too, so you buy one outdoor unit that works all year."},
    {"problem": "You want lower gas bills but don't trust a heat pump in February", "solution": "A hybrid setup answers that worry. The heat pump runs through the mild lakeshore months, and a 96% AFUE furnace takes over on the coldest nights. One thermostat decides which one runs, based on the outdoor temperature."},
    {"problem": "The basement is finished and you dread the mess", "solution": "Most of the work happens in the furnace room and outside. We lay floor protection along the path, reuse the existing ducts, and route refrigerant and condensate lines along joists or bulkheads you already have."},
