    {"problem": "A 1960s Aldershot bungalow has undersized ducts", "solution": "Older ducts were sized for a furnace, not for the airflow a heat pump needs in cooling mode. We measure static pressure and, where needed, upsize a return or a trunk section so the new system runs quietly."},
    {"problem": "Upstairs bedrooms in Millcroft stay warm on summer nights", "solution": "Bigger 1990s homes often have weak returns on the second floor. A variable-speed blower, plus balancing at the dampers, moves more air upstairs at a lower and quieter speed."},
