  ("Is a heat pump a good fit for a Burlington home?", "Yes, for most local homes. Lake-moderated winters let a cold-climate heat pump do most of the heating here, and models rated to -30°C keep working through cold snaps."),
  ("Should I pick an all-electric heat pump or a hybrid system in Burlington?", "A hybrid system suits most gas-heated homes that want a fuel backup, while an all-heat-pump setup suits owners who want to drop gas entirely. We price both so you can compare the upfront cost and the running cost."),
  ("Roughly what does heat pump installation in Burlington run, before rebates?", "Ducted cold-climate heat pumps start from $5,500 installed, and high-efficiency furnaces start from $3,300. Installed pricing depends on size and installation requirements, and both options come with a guaranteed written quote."),
  ("Will a heat pump install damage my finished basement?", "In most homes, no. We work from the furnace room, reuse the existing ducts and route lines through bulkheads or along joists, and we talk through any wall opening with you before we make it."),
